      "index": 0,
      "text": "Binary search is a divide-and-conquer algorithm that works on a sorted array. It finds an element by repeatedly dividing the search interval in half.\nHere's why it takes logarithmic time:\n1. Initial state: You have n elements to search through.\n2. Each step: The algorithm compares the target with the middle element.\n   - If the target is the middle element, we're done.\n   - If the target is smaller, we search the left half.\n   - If the target is larger, we search the right half.\n3. After each comparison, the search space is halved.",
